<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Musa ibn Nusayr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">640–716</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Musa ibn Nusayr was the Umayyad governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> who completed the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. His subordinate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a> crossed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> in 711 and defeated the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roderic">Roderic</a>; Musa followed in 712 with a larger army and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>, Mérida and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>. Recalled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in 714, he fell from favour with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> and died in obscurity.</p></div>
